fix(phase5): thread leftover prose into device search

The Phase 1 router dropped the free-text part whenever a device
identifier (M09192, TMV-400, etc.) was extracted, so questions like

  "X tengely golyós orsó csapágyak típusa és mennyisége, M09192 munkánál"

became a bare device filter and returned ALL tickets for that
device with no signal which one actually answered the question.
Pre-Phase-1, the LLM itself would have called search_existing_tickets
with both q and the device filter, getting properly ranked results.

Fix: in the device branches, compute a leftover prose string (text
with the device token stripped) and pass it as filters.q whenever
the leftover has at least 2 substantive tokens. Bare device
questions like "M09192" or "M09192 ticketjei" still hit
device_tickets_list without an over-restrictive q.

Tests: 4 new cases in 10-router.test.ts cover:
  - device + multi-token prose -> q set, device stripped from q
  - bare device identifier     -> no q
  - device + 1 generic word    -> no q (still too short)
  - device + 'leggyakoribb'    -> device_top_problem with q

Full suite: 294/294 pass (was 290), 1585 expects, tsc clean.
